ore than I want  European and British people to suffer  that's my view I don't none of us should  want that but I think there's definitely  a sense of  Pride that somehow Russian suffering  equals Russian leadership and I think  he's about to be shocked because this is  the 21st century and Russian people just  like European people don't want to go  through what they're about to go through  in terms of what is happening on the  ground do you have any understanding or  any information about why this Convoy  approaching Kiev appears to have stalled  is it do we think logistical issues  fueling for example or you know getting  getting supplies to them  or is it possibly a tactical thing to  wait well I think it's a combination of  all of what you above effectively that  what we have seen is that they weren't  properly their tactics weren't correct  they were doing things uh you know  thought they they were rather confident  they would take many of these cities in  a few hours rather than six days or  longer and when any army on the Move uh  has to do takes longer to do things your  logistical supply chain is stretched you  know if you if you're given enough  rations for two days and it takes you  six you suddenly got a problem and I  think what we've seen is a lot of those  issues are coming to Bear they've also  been surprised by the Ukrainian strength  of the resistance and indeed as a result  you know the ukrainians have been also  carrying out a very clever plan we've  seen footage we can't verify but we've  seen footage of you know ukrainians  using uavs to attack petrol uh train  convoys to go after logistical lines  we've seen railway lines blown up all  the things that you and I you know think  of about when it comes to resistance so  I think that is effectively coming home  to roost but it is also a switch in  Russian tactics I think the Russians  have realized that the ukrainians by  fighting are costing them lots and lots  of casualties and the Russians have  taken significant casualties uh far more  than they would have planned and I think  what they are therefore doing is trying  to switch tactics and what you're seeing  now is those heavy bombardments at night  they'll they'll try they won't come into  the cities as much they will I'm afraid  as we've seen tragically well the looks  of things carpet bomb cities uh  indiscriminately in some cases they will  fly their Air at night rather than  daytime because what we've seen is they  get shot down in the daytime and they  will try it slowly but surely try and  surround the cities and then either  bypass them or bombard them and I think  you know that is the brutality that I'm  afraid we are witnessing and it's going  to get worse I've worn before in your  program that that is you know the  Russian Doctrine is to get harder and  tougher and more indiscriminate and  that's why you know that tragic strike  on obviously the cemetery in the in the  Ascension of Kiev uh is exactly what we  should expect more of  you know you talked about carpet farm  and cluster Munitions have been used  thermobaric weapons have been used are  you confident that they have  uh we will collect the evidence on on a  range of those uh usage a number of  international Partners such as Canada  are quite rightly putting lots of effort  in collecting evidence if there was any  evidence of war crimes that would be  either presented to the international  criminal court or indeed countries on  their own are free to take certain  actions uh you know we have to you know  war crimes or anything else are done  based on evidence we've seen reports  we've certainly seen the deployment of  some of those weapon systems uh we  haven't verified the use but that's why  we will collect evidence for it and um  you know some of these weapon systems  are horrendous about a week ago we  summoned the defense attache from the  Russian Embassy to the ministry to  remind him of his obligations under the  Geneva Conventio